<item>
<title>▶ Does having protein really damage your kidneys?...</title>
<link>https://www.instagram.com/p/DgKkGMmgmAs/</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">instagram:https://www.instagram.com/p/DgKkGMmgmAs/</guid>
<pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:49:01 GMT</pubDate>
<dc:creator>Only What’s Needed · Instagram</dc:creator>
<category>Instagram</category>
<media:content url="https://www.instagram.com/p/DgKkGMmgmAs/media?size=l" medium="image"/>
<description><![CDATA[<video controls><source src="" poster="https://www.instagram.com/p/DgKkGMmgmAs/media?size=l" type="video/mp4"><img src="https://www.instagram.com/p/DgKkGMmgmAs/media?size=l" alt=""></video><br><br>Does having protein really damage your kidneys?<br />
<br />
Here&#039;s what you need to know:<br />
<br />
- When you consume protein, your body absorbs what&#039;s needed and also creates waste as a byproduct. Your kidneys filter out this waste from your blood.<br />
<br />
- So, when you eat more protein, your kidneys have more waste to filter. But they exist to do that exact job, so it doesn&#039;t automatically mean they&#039;re getting damaged.<br />
<br />
However, if you have an existing kidney condition, your protein requirements may be different. So it&#039;s always a good idea to check with your doctor before increasing your protein intake.<br />
<br />
Do share this video with someone who still believes protein damages kidneys!]]></description>
</item>
